# Parallel agent architectural coordination

Follow the mandatory [common AI-assisted development governance protocol](../../docs/engineering/AI_ASSISTED_DEVELOPMENT_GOVERNANCE.md#21-mandatory-parallel-agent-architectural-coordination) for Cursor, ChatGPT, Codex and other coding agents.

Before implementing shared functionality or dispatching overlapping work:

- Search existing implementations, extension points, relevant backlog items, open PRs and known active assignments by capability, not just file or class name.
- Reuse existing components. Establish one implementation owner and agreed contract for each overlapping shared capability before dependent implementation proceeds.
- Record ownership, scope, branch/PR, dependencies and verification in the existing shared task/PR plan. Do not create competing components or a second permanent registry.
- Parallelize independent changes. Coordinate shared contract changes and avoid overlapping writes; disclose unknown or inaccessible concurrent work.
- Before integration, recheck upstream and pending changes, review combined architectural impact and verify affected consumers against the integrated revision. Individual passing tests and conflict-free merges do not establish architectural compatibility.

Preserve the Architecture-Invariants and Shared-Component-Impact-Analysis rules, working-tree safety, test integrity, existing branch and merge authority, and authorized CI budgets. This rule does not authorize delegation or background work. The canonical governance document defines the full procedure; do not duplicate it here.

Mandatory procedural guidance, not an executable locking or global agent-discovery mechanism.
